<title>FRANCE: Peugeot sets wage rise of up to 2.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Peugeot sets wage rise of up to 2.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Automobiles Peugeot, part of the PSA Peugeot Citroen group, has proposed annual wage increases averaging 1.4 percent with the possibility of a further 1.3 percent in merit rises, a Peugeot spokesman said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The potential 2.7 percent increase, which compares with a wage rise of up to 3.5 percent in 1996, is conditional on a wage accord with the unions, the spokesman said. If an accord is not reached, the rise would be reduced to a maximum of 2.5 percent.</p>
</text>
